/**
 * About me art: a grimoire open on the desk, a quill beside it, a camp mug of coffee.
 * Three spreads, and each one opens with a problem:
 *  1. code: errors burst out of a buggy function (3 PROBLEMS)
 *  2. the plan: the to-dos fly off the page (OVERDUE)
 *  3. the power system: the tier chart falls apart (UNBALANCED)
 * Click the quill and it writes the fix; each problem clears and the stamp turns green.
 * Click the book to turn the page (and get the next problem); click the mug and it spills
 * across the notebook, then rights itself. Only one of the three happens at a time.
 * The scene is laid out at 760×520 and scaled to the column (notebook.ts sets --s).
 * Without JavaScript it's a still drawing of the first spread, fixed.
 * Pages: src/scripts/grimoire-pages.ts · logic: src/scripts/notebook.ts · styles: global.css ("grimoire")
 */
